---
description: Server-side enforcement, auth-derived scope, append-only tables
alwaysApply: true
---

# Security defaults

- Never implement access restrictions only in the frontend. Spec restrictions must be enforced server-side (middleware or DB); UI hide is secondary only.
- Never trust client-supplied jurisdiction/scope (district_id, state_id, inspector_id, etc.). Server-derived scope from the auth token always wins and silently overrides conflicting client values.
- Append-only tables (audit logs, report version history) must have no UPDATE/DELETE grant for application roles at the DB level — do not rely on "API has no route."
